.Dd October 24, 2026
.Dt AUGITE 1
.Os Augite DEVEL
.
.Sh NAME
.Nm augite
.Nd generate static sites for Git repositories
.
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar subcommand
.Ar arguments
.Nm
.Oo
.Fl h No \&|
.Fl "-help"
.Oc
.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
generates static HTML pages for Git repositories,
including commit logs,
diffs,
file contents,
references and Atom feeds.
File pages can be highlighted with TextMate grammars.
The generated files can be served by a web server without running
Augite on each request.
.Pp
The
.Ic git
executable must be available on
.Ev PATH .
Both bare repositories and repositories with working trees can
be used.
Pages describe committed content,
rather than uncommitted changes in the working tree.
.
.Sh SUBCOMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Xr augite-setup 1
.Xc
Sets or shows a repository’s description,
owner and clone URL.
.It Xo
.Xr augite-repo 1
.Xc
Generates one repository’s site.
.It Xo
.Xr augite-index 1
.Xc
Generates an index page listing repositories.
.El
.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Xo
.Fl h ,
.Fl "-help"
.Xc
Prints a usage summary and exits.
Each subcommand also accepts these options to show its own usage.
.El
.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits with status 0 on success,
including when help is requested,
and status 1 on an error.
.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Set repository metadata,
generate its pages and create an index:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ augite setup -d \(dqThe Analytical Engine\(dq --owner \(dqAda Lovelace\(dq /var/git/engine\&.git
$ augite repo -o public/engine /var/git/engine\&.git
$ augite index -o public /var/git/engine\&.git
.Ed
.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr augite-index 1 ,
.Xr augite-repo 1 ,
.Xr augite-setup 1 ,
.Xr git 1
.
